cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "dualmesh: the dual mesh control domain method for computational fluid dynamics and solid mechanics"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the method (see references)."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: LGPL-2.1-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/OWNER/dualmesh"
url: "https://dualmesh.readthedocs.io"
abstract: >-
  dualmesh solves boundary value problems of heat transfer, solid mechanics,
  structural mechanics and viscous incompressible flow with the dual mesh
  control domain method (DMCDM) of J. N. Reddy, and with the Galerkin finite
  element method from the same problem definition. The library is written in
  C++17 with Python bindings, is organized as a modular framework of kernels,
  boundary conditions and materials, and is verified against the published
  results of Reddy's book and against OpenFOAM.
keywords:
  - dual mesh control domain method
  - finite element method
  - finite volume method
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - solid mechanics
  - heat transfer
authors:
  - name: "The dualmesh developers"
references:
  - type: book
    title: "Computational Methods in Engineering: Finite Difference, Finite Volume, Finite Element, and Dual Mesh Control Domain Methods"
    authors:
      - family-names: Reddy
        given-names: "J. N."
    publisher:
      name: "CRC Press"
    year: 2024
